### =====================================================================
### END-TO-END (Phase 4): the catalog with CQRS, through the API gateway (port 8080)
###
###   writes (POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE) -> product-service -> MySQL
###        -> Debezium -> Kafka (cdc.product_db.*) -> product-read-service -> Elasticsearch
###   reads  (GET)                    -> product-read-service -> Elasticsearch
###
### Needs: infrastructure, auth-service, product-service, product-read-service, api-gateway,
###        and the connectors (scripts\register-connectors.ps1).
### Written for the VS Code "REST Client" extension. Run the requests IN ORDER.
### "wait" steps: a change reaches search after about a second (eventual consistency).
### =====================================================================

@gatewayUrl = http://localhost:8080

@vendorToken = {{vendorLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@categoryId = {{newCategory.response.body.$.data.id}}
@productId = {{newProduct.response.body.$.data.id}}
@imagePath = {{imageUpload.response.body.$.data.imageUrls[0]}}


### 1. vendor1 (Fresh Mart, store 1) logs in
# @name vendorLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "vendor1@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### 2. The admin logs in
# @name adminLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### 3. Admin creates a category (WRITE -> product-service)
# @name newCategory
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/admin/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bakery & Bread",
  "displayOrder": 6
}


### 4. Vendor adds a product to it (WRITE -> product-service; 50.00 - 10 % = 45.00)
# @name newProduct
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/products
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "categoryId": {{categoryId}},
  "name": "Whole Wheat Bread",
  "brand": "Modern",
  "sku": "FM-BRD-001",
  "unit": "G",
  "unitQuantity": 400,
  "price": 50.00,
  "discountPercentage": 10,
  "taxPercentage": 0
}


### 5. (wait) Customers find it by searching (READ -> product-read-service, Elasticsearch, no token)
# @wait 2
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products?q=bread


### 6. Vendor changes the price (50.00 - 20 % = 40.00)
PUT {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "categoryId": {{categoryId}},
  "name": "Whole Wheat Bread",
  "brand": "Modern",
  "sku": "FM-BRD-001",
  "unit": "G",
  "unitQuantity": 400,
  "price": 50.00,
  "discountPercentage": 20,
  "taxPercentage": 0
}


### 7. (wait) The search result shows the new price
# @wait 2
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{productId}}


### 8. Admin renames the category
PUT {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/admin/categories/{{categoryId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bakery",
  "displayOrder": 6
}


### 9. (wait) The product now shows the new category name; searching "bakery" finds it
# @wait 2
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products?q=bakery


### 10. Vendor uploads a product image
# @name imageUpload
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/products/{{productId}}/images
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=GroceryBoundary

--GroceryBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="sample-product.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./assets/sample-product.png
--GroceryBoundary--


### 11. Anyone can load the image (the URL from request 10, served through the gateway)
GET {{imagePath}}


### 12. Admin blocks the product (moderation)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/admin/products/{{productId}}/block
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 13. (wait) Customers can no longer see it -> 404
# @wait 2
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{productId}}


### 14. The vendor still sees it in their list, as BLOCKED
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/products?status=BLOCKED
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 15. Vendor deletes the product
DELETE {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 16. (wait) It is gone from the read model, even for the admin -> 404
# @wait 2
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/admin/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
